1
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:51,859
[2010 Haesol City
Superintendent's Cup Judo Tournament]

2
00:00:53,954 --> 00:00:55,803
[Sharp skills, strong mind! Go Haesol
Judo Team! Haesol's pride is on the line!]

3
00:00:55,803 --> 00:01:00,208
[Finals]
[Haesol High Jung Woo Jae : Yoon Ha Ru]

4
00:01:01,165 --> 00:01:03,457
<i>What is this? Is it a dream?</i>

5
00:01:04,459 --> 00:01:06,568
<i>2010?</i>

6
00:01:06,568 --> 00:01:07,770
Everyone in the center, please.

7
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:10,306
<i>What? Is he talking to me?</i>

8
00:01:10,306 --> 00:01:12,259
Player Yoon Ha Ru, what are you doing?

9
00:01:12,259 --> 00:01:13,867
Come on, onto the mat, please.

10
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:15,551
<i>Why is he telling me that?</i>

11
00:01:16,141 --> 00:01:18,654
<i>What is this?</i>

12
00:01:19,730 --> 00:01:21,430
<i>Woo Jae!</i>

13
00:01:23,018 --> 00:01:24,718
<i>Jung Woo Jae!</i>

14
00:01:29,357 --> 00:01:30,825
<i>What is this?</i>

15
00:01:30,825 --> 00:01:32,525
<i>Where am I?</i>

16
00:01:33,153 --> 00:01:34,853
<i>Mom? Dad?</i>

17
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:38,150
<i>Jung Woo Jae?</i>

18
00:01:40,913 --> 00:01:42,613
Woo Jae!

19
00:01:47,017 --> 00:01:49,170
- What the...
- What is he doing?

20
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:50,838
- What?
- Yoon Ha Ru?

21
00:01:50,838 --> 00:01:52,624
- What's going on?
- Ha Ru?

22
00:01:52,624 --> 00:01:54,448
He's just nervous. That must be it.

23
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:57,188
- It's just nerves.
- Surely, yeah.

24
00:01:59,465 --> 00:02:01,165
Hey!

25
00:02:03,269 --> 00:02:04,755
Start!

26
00:02:13,325 --> 00:02:15,051
Woo Jae, full point!

27
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,704
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

28
00:02:26,704 --> 00:02:28,404
You okay?

29
00:02:35,911 --> 00:02:38,095
Wait, are you crying?

30
00:02:38,095 --> 00:02:39,482
Huh?

31
00:02:42,513 --> 00:02:43,597
No way.

32
00:02:43,597 --> 00:02:46,662
Are you crying because you lost to me?

33
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,611
What?

34
00:02:51,525 --> 00:02:54,595
What am I... doing over there?

35
00:02:55,731 --> 00:02:57,851
What am I doing over there?

36
00:03:08,483 --> 00:03:10,687
Where do you think you're touching,
you bastard?

37
00:03:10,687 --> 00:03:12,387
What the heck!

38
00:03:31,848 --> 00:03:33,492
- Honey, come here, look!
- Honey...

39
00:03:33,492 --> 00:03:34,863
Ha Na is awake!

40
00:03:34,863 --> 00:03:36,216
Ha Ru, too!

41
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:38,382
Ha Ru, Ha Ru!

42
00:03:38,382 --> 00:03:39,994
Oh, thank goodness! Thank goodness!

43
00:03:39,994 --> 00:03:42,896
Doctor! They're awake!

44
00:03:42,896 --> 00:03:44,872
I'll go get someone, honey.

45
00:03:44,872 --> 00:03:46,109
Nurse!

46
00:03:46,109 --> 00:03:47,363
Ha Ru.

47
00:03:47,363 --> 00:03:48,611
Ha Na.

48
00:03:48,611 --> 00:03:50,163
Can you see me? It's Mom.

49
00:03:50,163 --> 00:03:52,366
Mom...

50
00:03:52,366 --> 00:03:54,743
Thank goodness, oh, good heavens!

51
00:03:54,743 --> 00:03:56,299
Everything's going to be fine
now that you're awake!

52
00:03:56,299 --> 00:03:58,532
- Oh, my sweet children!
- Mom...

53
00:04:00,092 --> 00:04:02,316
Yes, darling? What is it?

54
00:04:02,316 --> 00:04:04,016
Where is Woo Jae?

55
00:04:04,636 --> 00:04:08,703
He was... with me just now.

56
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:13,843
Did you have a dream about him?

57
00:04:13,843 --> 00:04:15,049
A dream?

58
00:04:15,049 --> 00:04:16,331
Ha Na.

59
00:04:16,331 --> 00:04:18,890
I'm sure Woo Jae is in a better place now.

60
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:21,302
He was a good boy.

61
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,040
That was a dream?

62
00:04:27,803 --> 00:04:29,743
That was just a dream?

63
00:04:31,192 --> 00:04:32,789
What's taking your dad so long anyway?

64
00:04:32,789 --> 00:04:34,949
He's supposed to be back with a doctor by now.

65
00:04:44,814 --> 00:04:46,514
I saw him, too.

66
00:04:47,433 --> 00:04:49,133
Jung Woo Jae.

67
00:04:56,384 --> 00:05:00,208
Do twins have matching dreams?
Is that even a thing?

68
00:05:01,405 --> 00:05:03,845
What a messed-up dream.

69
00:05:05,801 --> 00:05:07,368
The dream...

70
00:05:08,563 --> 00:05:10,804
It was so vivid.

71
00:05:12,407 --> 00:05:15,402
I could hear him breathe up close.

72
00:05:16,943 --> 00:05:19,340
I wish it lasted longer.

73
00:05:20,472 --> 00:05:23,370
We could've had more time together.

74
00:05:24,814 --> 00:05:27,107
I wish I never woke up.

75
00:05:29,308 --> 00:05:30,878
Huh?

76
00:05:33,714 --> 00:05:35,135
What?

77
00:05:39,489 --> 00:05:41,006
Hey.

78
00:05:41,006 --> 00:05:42,281
Yoon Ha Na.

79
00:05:42,281 --> 00:05:43,827
What?

80
00:05:43,827 --> 00:05:45,527
This is...

81
00:05:47,223 --> 00:05:48,860
What is this?

82
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:50,943
What are you talking about?

83
00:05:50,943 --> 00:05:52,074
It changed.

84
00:05:52,074 --> 00:05:53,774
What did?

85
00:05:56,047 --> 00:05:57,733
The medal!

86
00:05:57,733 --> 00:05:59,357
I got the gold medal that day, right?

87
00:05:59,357 --> 00:06:01,790
Now it's silver!

88
00:06:10,077 --> 00:06:11,545
Huh?

89
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:27,267
What in the...

90
00:06:29,904 --> 00:06:33,261
Did I... really do that?

91
00:06:33,261 --> 00:06:36,250
Wait, that's...

92
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,292
That's me!

93
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,691
Huh?

94
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:42,391
Rewind it one more time.

95
00:06:49,113 --> 00:06:51,044
So, what you're saying is...

96
00:06:51,044 --> 00:06:54,364
that that wasn't actually a dream?

97
00:06:54,364 --> 00:06:56,697
If it had been,
how would the medal have changed?

98
00:06:56,697 --> 00:06:58,370
And the video changed as well.

99
00:06:58,370 --> 00:07:00,530
It mysteriously disappeared, too, right?

100
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:02,671
It's suspicious, no?

101
00:07:02,671 --> 00:07:04,818
Maybe we're still dreaming?

102
00:07:08,306 --> 00:07:09,424
I guess not.

103
00:07:09,424 --> 00:07:11,831
It absolutely wasn't a dream.

104
00:07:11,831 --> 00:07:13,788
How does that make any sense?

105
00:07:13,788 --> 00:07:15,488
It makes no sense...

106
00:07:17,136 --> 00:07:19,558
- Or does it?
- Well, what if...

107
00:07:19,558 --> 00:07:21,052
it does make sense?

108
00:07:21,845 --> 00:07:22,857
Huh?

109
00:07:22,857 --> 00:07:24,657
If we can go back in time,

110
00:07:24,657 --> 00:07:27,857
and change the color of the medal...

111
00:07:27,857 --> 00:07:28,946
Then...

112
00:07:28,946 --> 00:07:30,363
Woo Jae.

113
00:07:30,363 --> 00:07:32,726
Maybe we could do the same with him.

114
00:07:40,133 --> 00:07:43,091
Wait, why isn't it working?

115
00:07:43,091 --> 00:07:44,791
How do I do this?

116
00:07:45,717 --> 00:07:47,417
Give it here.

117
00:07:49,839 --> 00:07:52,914
Have you lost it?
That thing's already old as bones!

118
00:07:54,052 --> 00:07:55,549
Sorry.

119
00:07:57,052 --> 00:07:59,117
Let's do a recap.

120
00:07:59,117 --> 00:08:00,621
Okay.

121
00:08:01,779 --> 00:08:04,066
We were on our way home...

122
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:06,879
When a truck hurtled our way.

123
00:08:06,879 --> 00:08:08,993
Then the camcorder started
playing back a video on its own.

124
00:08:08,993 --> 00:08:10,680
That's everything I can recall.

125
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,769
Do you remember anything else?

126
00:08:12,769 --> 00:08:14,890
I've got nothing after the truck.

127
00:08:14,890 --> 00:08:16,745
I don't know what you want me to say.

128
00:08:21,124 --> 00:08:22,824
And...

129
00:08:23,491 --> 00:08:25,128
When I came to,

130
00:08:25,128 --> 00:08:27,251
I was recording Woo Jae and me
with the camcorder.

131
00:08:27,251 --> 00:08:28,991
Well, not me, you.

132
00:08:28,991 --> 00:08:30,544
Anyway...

133
00:08:30,544 --> 00:08:32,544
I was recording. That's the point.

134
00:08:32,544 --> 00:08:36,190
Then, I saw the match end in,
what, 3 seconds with a full point.

135
00:08:36,190 --> 00:08:38,377
There were tears, Woo Jae was confused...

136
00:08:38,377 --> 00:08:41,196
Well, I thought it was all a dream.
But something was clearly off.

137
00:08:41,196 --> 00:08:43,912
So I was feeling myself up a little,

138
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:46,277
and felt something weird on my chest...

139
00:08:46,277 --> 00:08:47,911
That's enough, I get it.

140
00:08:47,911 --> 00:08:50,268
I saw it with my own eyes.

141
00:08:50,268 --> 00:08:51,710
I was shocked, too, you know.

142
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:54,584
That's why I dropped the camcorder,
and that was that.

143
00:08:55,210 --> 00:08:58,565
And so we returned to the present, right?

144
00:09:05,257 --> 00:09:07,067
- Ready?
- Yeah.

145
00:09:07,067 --> 00:09:08,767
Here goes.

146
00:09:09,356 --> 00:09:11,615
One, two, three.

147
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:24,599
Dang it. It's not working.

148
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:28,219
Ow, my legs.

149
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:31,658
I guess your legs are too short to hurt, huh?

150
00:09:57,643 --> 00:09:59,527
It's not working.

151
00:09:59,527 --> 00:10:00,731
Dive in.

152
00:10:00,731 --> 00:10:02,431
Dive in?

153
00:10:03,363 --> 00:10:05,063
Okay. Sure...

154
00:10:13,356 --> 00:10:15,702
No, hold on a little longer!

155
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:25,652
I almost drowned!

156
00:10:51,546 --> 00:10:54,537
It looks... pretty deep, huh?

157
00:10:54,537 --> 00:10:56,624
Well...

158
00:10:56,624 --> 00:10:59,052
We need to jump at the same time.

159
00:10:59,052 --> 00:11:00,830
Of course.

160
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:03,139
At the same time. Yeah, I know.

161
00:11:03,139 --> 00:11:05,377
Together, yeah, obviously.

162
00:11:05,377 --> 00:11:07,581
- Are you scared?
- Of course I...

163
00:11:12,735 --> 00:11:14,230
Scared?

164
00:11:14,230 --> 00:11:16,963
Wow, really, Yoon Ha Na?

165
00:11:16,963 --> 00:11:18,340
This is Yoon Ha Ru we're talking about.

166
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:21,284
Your big brother doesn't feel fear at all.

167
00:11:21,284 --> 00:11:24,265
Honestly, I don't know
what that word even means.

168
00:11:25,339 --> 00:11:27,237
Your left leg has been shaking non-stop
for the last few minutes.

169
00:11:27,237 --> 00:11:28,596
Huh?

170
00:11:32,669 --> 00:11:34,117
I'm not shaking.

171
00:11:34,117 --> 00:11:35,614
I'm just getting the engine started.

172
00:11:35,614 --> 00:11:37,112
What's it to you?

173
00:11:39,944 --> 00:11:43,133
Why is the water... so pitch black?

174
00:11:43,133 --> 00:11:46,413
It's making me imagine things
lurking underneath the surface.

175
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:52,910
You sure have the ample imagination
of the actress that you are.

176
00:11:52,910 --> 00:11:54,649
This is an indoor pool.

177
00:11:54,649 --> 00:11:56,335
There's nothing in the water.

178
00:11:56,335 --> 00:11:57,806
And I have to tell you...

179
00:11:57,806 --> 00:11:59,350
I'm a very good swimmer.

180
00:11:59,350 --> 00:12:02,803
You know that I was in the
children's swimming team.

181
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:08,388
Actually, I'm scared, too.

182
00:12:09,722 --> 00:12:11,833
But...

183
00:12:11,833 --> 00:12:14,611
As long as there's even a slim chance of hope,

184
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:17,211
I'd do anything.

185
00:12:21,216 --> 00:12:23,213
Me too.

186
00:12:23,213 --> 00:12:25,225
Because it's Jung Woo Jae.

187
00:12:26,493 --> 00:12:27,916
Yeah.

188
00:12:27,916 --> 00:12:29,856
Because it's Jung Woo Jae.

189
00:13:00,879 --> 00:13:03,620
<i>My heart is racing.</i>

190
00:13:04,437 --> 00:13:06,487
Hold your breath, Yoon Ha Ru.

191
00:13:06,487 --> 00:13:07,948
Got it.

192
00:13:09,844 --> 00:13:13,000
<i>Out of fear, or from excitement...</i>

193
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,821
<i>I'll never know for sure.</i>

194
00:13:18,713 --> 00:13:20,894
<i>But I don't hesitate for even a moment...</i>

195
00:13:21,906 --> 00:13:23,988
<i>as I dive into the emptiness below.</i>

196
00:13:42,426 --> 00:13:44,032
<i>Into Jung Woo Jae.</i>

197
00:13:47,473 --> 00:13:49,173
<i>Into you.</i>

198
00:14:01,487 --> 00:14:02,943
<i>What's this?</i>

199
00:14:05,447 --> 00:14:07,147
<i>What's going on?</i>

200
00:14:08,699 --> 00:14:10,399
<i>What is happening?</i>

201
00:14:12,305 --> 00:14:14,536
What the...

202
00:14:14,536 --> 00:14:15,713
What?

203
00:14:15,713 --> 00:14:17,259
What is that?

204
00:14:20,696 --> 00:14:22,396
That scared me!

205
00:14:23,426 --> 00:14:25,159
Darn it, Yoon Ha Na!

206
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:30,926
You! What's up with this face?
In the middle of the night, no less!

207
00:14:30,926 --> 00:14:33,080
I thought I crossed the Styx or something!

208
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,661
Yoon Ha Ru?

209
00:14:35,563 --> 00:14:41,324
Ah, I was preparing for
an audition on this day.

210
00:14:41,998 --> 00:14:43,473
The makeup looks pretty good.

211
00:14:43,473 --> 00:14:45,173
It's captured the vibe well.

212
00:14:46,256 --> 00:14:48,123
Oh, my heart.

213
00:14:53,788 --> 00:14:56,216
It's 2010.

214
00:14:56,216 --> 00:14:58,051
Are you serious?

215
00:15:01,599 --> 00:15:03,143
This is the one, right?

216
00:15:03,143 --> 00:15:04,843
The time machine?

217
00:15:09,669 --> 00:15:12,149
December 31st, 2010...

218
00:15:12,149 --> 00:15:13,524
That's the date of the second video.

219
00:15:13,524 --> 00:15:15,509
We made it.

220
00:15:16,687 --> 00:15:19,516
We actually traveled back in time?

221
00:15:19,516 --> 00:15:21,143
Yes.

222
00:15:21,143 --> 00:15:23,210
Wait, what?

223
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:25,497
Huh? What's wrong?

224
00:15:25,497 --> 00:15:27,197
We're in some deep trouble, then.

225
00:15:27,884 --> 00:15:30,183
Real deep trouble.

226
00:15:30,183 --> 00:15:31,883
Why? What is it?

227
00:15:35,672 --> 00:15:38,111
I am so gosh darn charmingly handsome.

228
00:15:39,490 --> 00:15:41,126
Do you actually want to cross the Styx?

229
00:15:41,126 --> 00:15:42,837
This skin...

230
00:15:42,837 --> 00:15:44,890
No amount of product or treatment
could ever recreate this.

231
00:15:44,890 --> 00:15:46,855
This is the real thing, real baby-soft skin!

232
00:15:46,855 --> 00:15:48,418
Get off me!

233
00:15:48,418 --> 00:15:50,951
You are one unhinged bastard!

234
00:15:52,633 --> 00:15:55,049
I should be the one on the big screen, not you.

235
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:58,174
It's Woo Jae!

236
00:15:58,174 --> 00:16:00,009
What?

237
00:16:00,009 --> 00:16:02,510
<i>Meet me at the place at 11:20.</i>

238
00:16:05,095 --> 00:16:07,756
Wait for me!

239
00:16:07,756 --> 00:16:11,012
Ugh, your hair is annoying!
I should just chop it off!

240
00:16:18,777 --> 00:16:20,072
You can cut it if you dare.

241
00:16:20,072 --> 00:16:22,341
I'll fill up on grilled pork belly
right before the national team trial,

242
00:16:22,341 --> 00:16:24,658
so that you never pass the
competition in the first place.

243
00:16:24,658 --> 00:16:27,112
You'll never even bear the Taegeuk symbol.

244
00:16:28,921 --> 00:16:30,578
Where are you even going?

245
00:16:30,578 --> 00:16:31,721
I don't know.

246
00:16:31,721 --> 00:16:33,513
It's too late to just walk off
without a clear destination!

247
00:16:33,513 --> 00:16:36,384
Well, Woo Jae wants to meet up!
I can't just sit around doing nothing!

248
00:16:37,150 --> 00:16:39,363
December 31st...

249
00:16:39,363 --> 00:16:41,664
What were we doing that day?

250
00:16:41,664 --> 00:16:43,026
Why did we meet up?

251
00:16:43,026 --> 00:16:44,181
December... 31st...

252
00:16:44,181 --> 00:16:46,673
It's the last day of the year, so...

253
00:16:47,819 --> 00:16:49,519
- The beach!
- The beach!

254
00:16:50,317 --> 00:16:52,453
Wait, help me tie my hair up first!

255
00:16:52,453 --> 00:16:54,257
I'm seriously going to cut it off!

256
00:16:54,257 --> 00:16:55,957
I'm not bluffing!

257
00:17:01,261 --> 00:17:02,518
He's not here.

258
00:17:02,518 --> 00:17:03,875
Is this not the place?

259
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:05,726
No, it is.

260
00:17:05,726 --> 00:17:07,636
This is the place, but...

261
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,842
It's past 11:50 now.

262
00:17:10,842 --> 00:17:12,840
So why isn't he here?

263
00:17:13,768 --> 00:17:15,899
Where are you, Jung Woo Jae?

264
00:17:15,899 --> 00:17:17,831
Wait, I'll call him.

265
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,570
Hey, Ha Na.

266
00:17:42,321 --> 00:17:44,021
<i>Jung Woo Jae...</i>

267
00:17:49,990 --> 00:17:52,181
Jung Woo Jae, you bastard!

268
00:17:52,181 --> 00:17:55,253
Jung Woo Jae, where the heck were you?

269
00:17:55,253 --> 00:17:57,930
Where were you? Tell me!

270
00:17:57,930 --> 00:18:00,243
We were supposed to meet
in front of the campus, remember?

271
00:18:00,243 --> 00:18:02,616
I was waiting for you, but you never came,
so I came for you.

272
00:18:02,616 --> 00:18:04,896
Why are you guys here?

273
00:18:04,896 --> 00:18:06,194
Are you feeling okay?

274
00:18:06,194 --> 00:18:08,738
No broken bones? No injuries?

275
00:18:08,738 --> 00:18:10,296
I'm fine.

276
00:18:11,116 --> 00:18:13,694
Hey. What's wrong with Ha Na?

277
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:21,021
What's up with you?

278
00:18:42,114 --> 00:18:43,372
Three...

279
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,492
Two...

280
00:18:44,492 --> 00:18:46,379
One! There it is.

281
00:18:46,379 --> 00:18:48,079
Happy New Year, guys!

282
00:18:49,219 --> 00:18:50,745
I guess.

283
00:18:53,109 --> 00:18:54,897
Hey, what's going on with you, Yoon Ha Ru?

284
00:18:54,897 --> 00:18:57,224
Why are you so unenthusiastic?

285
00:18:59,909 --> 00:19:02,800
Oh, am I supposed to be doing something?

286
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,179
Well, no.

287
00:19:04,179 --> 00:19:06,413
Not really, I guess.

288
00:19:06,413 --> 00:19:09,132
This is so fun!

289
00:19:09,132 --> 00:19:10,248
Yeah, guys!

290
00:19:10,248 --> 00:19:12,495
Let's have a super happy new year!
Lots of luck for everyone!

291
00:19:12,495 --> 00:19:13,700
We're seniors now, seniors!

292
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:16,020
We're 19 years old now!

293
00:19:17,510 --> 00:19:20,033
- What's up with Ha Na today?
- This is so awesome!

294
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:21,733
I don't know.

295
00:19:22,689 --> 00:19:26,032
She's acting a bit strange today.

296
00:19:26,894 --> 00:19:28,962
Watch your step!

297
00:19:34,414 --> 00:19:36,487
She's adorable.

298
00:19:36,487 --> 00:19:38,472
- What?
- She's...

299
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,436
No... nothing...

300
00:19:42,436 --> 00:19:44,816
Ha Na. She's...

301
00:19:44,816 --> 00:19:47,201
I said she's being particularly silly today.

302
00:19:47,201 --> 00:19:48,712
See? It's ridiculous.

303
00:19:48,712 --> 00:19:50,789
Something's up with her today.

304
00:19:50,789 --> 00:19:52,846
She's just being so silly today.

305
00:19:55,610 --> 00:19:57,470
Come on, this way!

306
00:19:57,470 --> 00:19:59,170
Alright, alright!

307
00:20:03,651 --> 00:20:04,789
Hey.

308
00:20:04,789 --> 00:20:06,489
Keep it together, will you?

309
00:20:07,519 --> 00:20:08,621
You're Yoon Ha Na now.

310
00:20:08,621 --> 00:20:11,232
Yoon Ha Na, the world-famous actress,
not the wild beast Yoon Ha Ru.

311
00:20:11,232 --> 00:20:13,006
I know!

312
00:20:13,006 --> 00:20:14,536
Woo Jae is giving you weird looks!

313
00:20:14,536 --> 00:20:16,462
Stop acting like an imbecile!

314
00:20:16,462 --> 00:20:17,610
Imbecile?

315
00:20:17,610 --> 00:20:19,131
I'm the national judo team's treasure,

316
00:20:19,131 --> 00:20:22,328
and the world's best judo player,
Sir Yoon Ha Ru!

317
00:20:29,592 --> 00:20:31,720
You should try your best to act like yourself,

318
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,223
and I as myself, don't you think?

319
00:20:34,837 --> 00:20:35,945
Hey, you.

320
00:20:35,945 --> 00:20:37,633
Are you embarrassed by me or something?

321
00:20:37,633 --> 00:20:41,281
Of course I am, what kind of question is that?
You're acting out of character in my body!

322
00:20:45,850 --> 00:20:47,734
Besides...

323
00:20:49,724 --> 00:20:51,424
I'm just scared.

324
00:20:52,665 --> 00:20:54,601
What if some small action...

325
00:20:55,636 --> 00:20:59,548
ends up irreversibly changing our past?

326
00:21:00,135 --> 00:21:01,261
You know.

327
00:21:01,261 --> 00:21:02,372
That's how it goes in movies.

328
00:21:02,372 --> 00:21:05,216
Just think about how the medal changed.

329
00:21:05,216 --> 00:21:08,488
We can save Jung Woo Jae.

330
00:21:12,783 --> 00:21:14,241
Okay.

331
00:21:30,559 --> 00:21:33,509
You must've been starving.

332
00:21:36,932 --> 00:21:39,476
Hey, will you slow down?

333
00:21:39,476 --> 00:21:42,396
All this food you're shoveling
in your mouth right now...

334
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:45,091
are you even keeping track
of how many calories that is?

335
00:21:45,091 --> 00:21:46,259
This is my first meal of the day!

336
00:21:46,259 --> 00:21:49,316
I'll just work out and burn it off,
so stop nagging me!

337
00:21:52,338 --> 00:21:53,675
You should slow down, though.

338
00:21:53,675 --> 00:21:55,375
Here, drink some water, too.

339
00:22:00,537 --> 00:22:01,651
Guys...

340
00:22:01,651 --> 00:22:03,469
I need to use the toilet.

341
00:22:03,469 --> 00:22:05,415
Agh, I'm about to poop my pants!

342
00:22:07,022 --> 00:22:09,044
What, right now? It's dangerous in the dark.

343
00:22:09,044 --> 00:22:12,200
- Do you want me to come with?
- Stop talking, it's peeking out!

344
00:22:12,798 --> 00:22:13,904
Ha Na!

345
00:22:13,904 --> 00:22:16,369
What does he think he's doing?

346
00:22:23,016 --> 00:22:25,074
Ha Na! That's the men's room!

347
00:22:27,170 --> 00:22:29,199
No, no, I told you I'm not drunk!

348
00:22:29,199 --> 00:22:30,534
I'm not drunk, I'm fine...

349
00:22:30,534 --> 00:22:32,490
Stop there for a second.

350
00:22:32,490 --> 00:22:34,169
All the toilets are backed up.

351
00:22:34,169 --> 00:22:35,586
Everything's broken in there.

352
00:22:35,586 --> 00:22:36,934
Sorry for the inconvenience.

353
00:22:36,934 --> 00:22:39,240
Did I poop too much? What if I clogged it?

354
00:22:53,529 --> 00:22:55,920
<i>I don't know what Jung Woo Jae is wishing for,</i>

355
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:57,190
<i>but whatever it is...</i>

356
00:22:57,190 --> 00:22:59,280
<i>I wish for it to come true.</i>

357
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:00,500
<i>Please...</i>

358
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:02,052
<i>Please.</i>

359
00:23:09,825 --> 00:23:11,702
What did you wish for?

360
00:23:11,702 --> 00:23:13,172
Hey! You're not supposed to tell.

361
00:23:13,172 --> 00:23:14,293
It won't come true!

362
00:23:14,293 --> 00:23:16,556
That's not how it works.

363
00:23:16,556 --> 00:23:19,612
Come on, tell me.
I could help make it come true.

364
00:23:21,325 --> 00:23:23,589
Well, I suppose you could help, yeah.

365
00:23:23,589 --> 00:23:25,252
What is it?

366
00:23:25,252 --> 00:23:27,123
The national team trial
is being held this year.

367
00:23:27,123 --> 00:23:29,163
I want to make it on the team with you.

368
00:23:29,163 --> 00:23:30,563
Yoon Ha Ru.

369
00:23:32,149 --> 00:23:33,739
- Huh?
- Well? Answer me.

370
00:23:33,739 --> 00:23:34,970
Don't you want to?

371
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:37,553
- Well...
- Of course!

372
00:23:38,740 --> 00:23:40,171
Don't even worry about it!

373
00:23:40,171 --> 00:23:44,093
You and I, we'll make it in. Whatever it takes.

374
00:23:44,093 --> 00:23:45,557
Huh? Ha Na?

375
00:23:45,557 --> 00:23:47,257
What do you mean, you and me?

376
00:23:49,114 --> 00:23:50,385
Oh, no, no.

377
00:23:50,385 --> 00:23:52,135
I meant, you and Yoon Ha Ru. You two.

378
00:23:52,135 --> 00:23:53,835
You'll make it in.

379
00:23:54,637 --> 00:23:56,337
You got me there.

380
00:24:09,226 --> 00:24:10,983
About Woo Jae...

381
00:24:10,983 --> 00:24:13,199
When did he stop judo again?

382
00:24:13,808 --> 00:24:17,333
Right before the national team trial, so...

383
00:24:17,333 --> 00:24:19,569
I guess around May?

384
00:24:19,569 --> 00:24:21,266
He hurt his shoulder.

385
00:24:21,266 --> 00:24:22,897
That's why he quit, right?

386
00:24:22,897 --> 00:24:24,765
Did it happen during practice?

387
00:24:25,761 --> 00:24:27,109
I think...

388
00:24:27,109 --> 00:24:29,669
He just appeared with a cast
on his arm one day.

389
00:24:31,325 --> 00:24:32,920
Are you sure you're a good friend to him?

390
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,600
You're his friend, too, you know!

391
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:36,300
But you had no clue, either!

392
00:24:38,713 --> 00:24:40,108
Well, this time around...

393
00:24:40,108 --> 00:24:42,478
Let's figure that out first.

394
00:24:42,478 --> 00:24:44,321
And then what?

395
00:24:44,321 --> 00:24:46,505
That way, we can prevent it from happening.

396
00:24:46,505 --> 00:24:48,442
That way...

397
00:24:48,442 --> 00:24:51,033
he'll never have to quit judo.

398
00:24:54,022 --> 00:24:55,679
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

399
00:24:55,679 --> 00:24:57,031
Okay.

400
00:25:08,716 --> 00:25:13,730
[Our dream, a brighter 2011]

401
00:25:15,947 --> 00:25:17,647
It's good.

402
00:25:20,263 --> 00:25:21,601
Oh, you're back.

403
00:25:21,601 --> 00:25:23,972
Wow, Woo Jae! How handsome you are!

404
00:25:23,972 --> 00:25:25,509
What a charming young man!

405
00:25:25,509 --> 00:25:26,698
Honey, what about me?

406
00:25:26,698 --> 00:25:28,775
Am I charming, too?

407
00:25:30,833 --> 00:25:32,364
I guess not.

408
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:33,916
Anyhow!

409
00:25:33,916 --> 00:25:35,622
Did you guys enjoy the sunrise?

410
00:25:35,622 --> 00:25:36,833
Did you take pictures?

411
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:39,033
Wash your hands, your dad made tteokguk.

412
00:25:39,033 --> 00:25:40,773
- Mom!
- Dad!

413
00:25:40,773 --> 00:25:42,110
What is it now?

414
00:25:42,110 --> 00:25:43,325
Don't you like it?

415
00:25:43,325 --> 00:25:44,607
I did a good job on it.

416
00:25:44,607 --> 00:25:45,961
No, it's not that.

417
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:49,767
I can't believe how the two of you look!

418
00:25:49,767 --> 00:25:51,774
This is unreal!

419
00:25:51,774 --> 00:25:53,267
This is just...

420
00:25:53,267 --> 00:25:54,781
Mom, your skin!

421
00:25:54,781 --> 00:25:58,378
Holy moly guacamole, that's gnarly!

422
00:26:00,087 --> 00:26:02,143
What did you say? Hole-y? Mole-y?

423
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:03,865
And what, gnarled?

424
00:26:03,865 --> 00:26:05,941
Not you too, Ha Na!

425
00:26:05,941 --> 00:26:08,328
No, Mom! It's a compliment! A compliment!

426
00:26:08,328 --> 00:26:09,744
Yoon Ha Na, come here!

427
00:26:09,744 --> 00:26:10,768
I said come here!

428
00:26:10,768 --> 00:26:12,880
Did you take after Ha Ru?

429
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:14,238
Huh? Come here!

430
00:26:14,238 --> 00:26:15,940
- Mom, Mom!
- How dare you call me gnarled!

431
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:17,121
- It's a compliment!
- Come here right now!

432
00:26:17,121 --> 00:26:19,165
- No, I was complimenting you!
- It's a compliment...

433
00:26:19,165 --> 00:26:20,865
Eat up, everyone.

434
00:26:22,021 --> 00:26:24,250
Woah, it's gosh dang tummylicious!

435
00:26:25,555 --> 00:26:26,926
Yoon Ha Na!

436
00:26:26,926 --> 00:26:29,179
What do you mean by that now?

437
00:26:30,448 --> 00:26:31,877
It means it's really good.

438
00:26:31,877 --> 00:26:32,901
It's just what we say.

439
00:26:32,901 --> 00:26:34,221
Yeah, that's right.

440
00:26:34,221 --> 00:26:36,305
- Is this true?
- Yes.

441
00:26:38,655 --> 00:26:40,488
Come on, honey.

442
00:26:40,488 --> 00:26:41,512
It's just how kids are.

443
00:26:41,512 --> 00:26:43,448
We were young once, too, right?

444
00:26:43,448 --> 00:26:45,301
It's just how teens talk. Their lingo.

445
00:26:45,301 --> 00:26:46,695
They'll grow out of it.

446
00:26:46,695 --> 00:26:48,955
"Grow out of it?"

447
00:26:48,955 --> 00:26:51,501
You still say stuff like rad and bonkers.

448
00:26:51,501 --> 00:26:53,908
- Old habits die hard, and...
- Oh, look, meat fritters.

449
00:26:53,908 --> 00:26:56,183
Your favorite, see?

450
00:26:58,454 --> 00:27:01,228
Aw, you look lovely when you eat.

451
00:27:01,228 --> 00:27:02,928
It tastes great, yes.

452
00:27:03,707 --> 00:27:04,731
- Dad.
- Yes?

453
00:27:04,731 --> 00:27:06,142
This is an amazing meal.

454
00:27:06,142 --> 00:27:08,301
Well, I am a good cook, see?

455
00:27:08,301 --> 00:27:09,875
What do you guys think? Am I rad?

456
00:27:09,875 --> 00:27:11,722
Yeah, radical!

457
00:27:11,722 --> 00:27:13,175
Bonkers!

458
00:27:13,175 --> 00:27:14,668
Ha Ru, did you finish packing yet?

459
00:27:14,668 --> 00:27:16,529
Packing? For what?

460
00:27:19,062 --> 00:27:21,215
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

461
00:27:21,215 --> 00:27:23,593
You're leaving for the
training camp in two days!

462
00:27:23,593 --> 00:27:25,359
I told you to get ready beforehand!

463
00:27:25,359 --> 00:27:27,299
You never listen, do you?

464
00:27:27,299 --> 00:27:29,675
Hurry up and finish eating! You need to pack!

465
00:27:31,706 --> 00:27:34,540
Honey, calm down and have another fritter...

466
00:27:35,193 --> 00:27:37,317
Oh, you've already got one.

467
00:27:38,308 --> 00:27:40,839
<i>You should tell me right away
if you changed your number.</i>

468
00:27:40,839 --> 00:27:43,202
<i>Son. Where are you?</i>

469
00:27:45,456 --> 00:27:47,156
[Haesol High Judo Team Winter Camp]
Attention!

470
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:50,746
There is only one goal
in this winter training camp.

471
00:27:50,746 --> 00:27:52,273
You are not only a team on the mat.

472
00:27:52,273 --> 00:27:55,552
You will eat, sleep, and even use the toilet...
as if you are one single organism.

473
00:27:55,552 --> 00:27:58,585
Therefore, you will stay in rooms of four.
No exceptions.

474
00:27:58,585 --> 00:28:00,160
- Oh, crap.
- Any objections?

475
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:01,577
- No, sir!
- No, sir!

476
00:28:01,577 --> 00:28:04,902
Good. Now, take off to unpack and settle in.
You will return here after 30 minutes.

477
00:28:04,902 --> 00:28:05,959
Understood?

478
00:28:05,959 --> 00:28:07,659
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

479
00:28:11,413 --> 00:28:13,113
We're in the same room.

480
00:28:13,945 --> 00:28:15,313
Oh, okay...

481
00:28:15,313 --> 00:28:16,696
Us, too.

482
00:28:24,225 --> 00:28:25,489
<i>Hey, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

483
00:28:25,489 --> 00:28:26,933
<i>Listen up carefully.</i>

484
00:28:26,933 --> 00:28:30,646
<i>Where you will be going tomorrow
is no ordinary training camp.</i>

485
00:28:30,646 --> 00:28:33,835
<i>That place is like the wilderness.
A safari, if you will.</i>

486
00:28:34,426 --> 00:28:35,450
<i>A safari?</i>

487
00:28:35,450 --> 00:28:36,478
<i>But do not fear!</i>

488
00:28:36,478 --> 00:28:40,623
<i>For I, your big brother, will teach you
all the essentials of survival.</i>

489
00:28:40,623 --> 00:28:41,953
<i>First off.</i>

490
00:28:41,953 --> 00:28:44,072
<i>The smell.</i>

491
00:28:44,072 --> 00:28:45,242
<i>Smell?</i>

492
00:28:45,242 --> 00:28:47,019
<i>The moment you set foot in that room...</i>

493
00:28:47,019 --> 00:28:50,130
<i>you will learn what hell is like.</i>

494
00:28:50,974 --> 00:28:52,364
<i>You've got to be exaggerating.</i>

495
00:28:52,364 --> 00:28:54,436
<i>You know Han Soo Hyuk, right?</i>

496
00:28:54,436 --> 00:28:56,090
<i>Han Soo Hyuk?</i>

497
00:28:57,203 --> 00:29:00,249
<i>The guy who quit judo
and came to my university...</i>

498
00:29:00,249 --> 00:29:01,289
<i>That Han Soo Hyuk?</i>

499
00:29:01,289 --> 00:29:02,399
<i>Well? What about him?</i>

500
00:29:02,399 --> 00:29:04,510
<i>What does he have to do with this?</i>

501
00:29:09,759 --> 00:29:12,233
<i>If you are condemned to a room with him...</i>

502
00:29:12,233 --> 00:29:14,675
<i>Well, you truly are doomed.</i>

503
00:29:22,393 --> 00:29:24,305
[Alarms off, please!]

504
00:29:24,305 --> 00:29:25,864
[Han Soo Hyuk]
[Yoon Ha Ru]

505
00:29:40,522 --> 00:29:42,066
What's wrong?

506
00:29:42,066 --> 00:29:45,066
<i>He has rhinitis, so his nose is always stuffy,
and he can't smell very well.</i>

507
00:29:45,066 --> 00:29:46,473
<i>Maybe that's why, but...</i>

508
00:29:46,473 --> 00:29:47,990
You!

509
00:29:48,646 --> 00:29:50,912
When did you last wash your uniform?

510
00:29:53,165 --> 00:29:54,189
Hey.

511
00:29:54,189 --> 00:29:55,847
Want a bite?

512
00:29:55,847 --> 00:29:57,673
<i>He doesn't do his laundry.</i>

513
00:29:57,673 --> 00:29:59,005
<i>As you already know, however...</i>

514
00:29:59,005 --> 00:30:00,813
<i>He's a good kid.</i>

515
00:30:00,813 --> 00:30:01,722
It's good bread.

516
00:30:01,722 --> 00:30:02,726
<i>And now.</i>

517
00:30:02,726 --> 00:30:05,072
<i>Pyo Gyeong Woo.</i>

518
00:30:05,072 --> 00:30:06,549
<i>I know Gyeong Woo.</i>

519
00:30:06,549 --> 00:30:09,442
<i>He's the son of the master
of that training center we went to as children.</i>

520
00:30:09,442 --> 00:30:12,629
<i>Starting tomorrow,
your eyes will be forced to witness...</i>

521
00:30:12,629 --> 00:30:14,690
<i>the parade of muscles.</i>

522
00:30:14,690 --> 00:30:16,819
<i>"Parade of muscles?"</i>

523
00:30:17,838 --> 00:30:20,056
- Get it out of my face.
- But it's really good.

524
00:30:37,501 --> 00:30:38,543
What...

525
00:30:38,543 --> 00:30:40,105
What are you doing?

526
00:30:42,502 --> 00:30:43,773
Hey.

527
00:30:45,137 --> 00:30:48,680
Pyo Gyeong Woo, sir,
reporting today's sick gains.

528
00:30:51,444 --> 00:30:53,346
- What's going on?
- How do you like them?

529
00:30:53,346 --> 00:30:55,251
<i>Our dear Gyeong Woo is, how should I say this?</i>

530
00:30:55,251 --> 00:30:57,218
<i>He's like a big dog who likes praise.</i>

531
00:30:57,218 --> 00:30:58,708
<i>Just think of him as that.</i>

532
00:30:58,708 --> 00:31:00,239
<i>He's a good kid, too. He doesn't mean any harm.</i>

533
00:31:00,239 --> 00:31:02,164
Here, my external oblique. Feel it.

534
00:31:02,164 --> 00:31:03,233
Come on, won't you feel it?

535
00:31:03,233 --> 00:31:04,933
My rectus abdominis...

536
00:31:07,083 --> 00:31:09,667
I've been doing low-rises...

537
00:31:16,801 --> 00:31:18,501
Salute!

538
00:31:26,794 --> 00:31:28,257
Oh, hello.

539
00:31:29,600 --> 00:31:31,300
Hello.

540
00:31:36,503 --> 00:31:38,067
<i>Also,</i>

541
00:31:38,067 --> 00:31:39,948
<i>this is the most important of them all.</i>

542
00:31:40,623 --> 00:31:41,767
<i>There's more?</i>

543
00:31:41,767 --> 00:31:43,600
<i>Jung Woo Jae.</i>

544
00:31:45,046 --> 00:31:46,723
<i>Keep an eye on him.</i>

545
00:31:46,723 --> 00:31:48,654
<i>If he's secretive, dig deeper.</i>

546
00:31:48,654 --> 00:31:50,894
<i>If he says he's fine, don't believe him.</i>

547
00:31:52,323 --> 00:31:54,027
<i>This time...</i>

548
00:31:54,027 --> 00:31:56,602
<i>We need to figure it out faster than him.</i>

549
00:31:56,602 --> 00:31:57,626
<i>Okay.</i>

550
00:31:57,626 --> 00:31:58,796
<i>Got it?</i>

551
00:31:58,796 --> 00:32:00,020
<i>Yeah.</i>

552
00:32:00,020 --> 00:32:01,887
<i>Are you done packing?</i>

553
00:32:01,887 --> 00:32:03,645
<i>What good is that going to do?</i>

554
00:32:03,645 --> 00:32:05,179
<i>Don't take hour-long showers
while you're there, understood?</i>

555
00:32:05,179 --> 00:32:07,973
<i>I just take longer showers than most, okay?</i>

556
00:32:07,973 --> 00:32:11,384
<i>Take stuff like this, for working out.</i>

557
00:32:14,174 --> 00:32:16,513
<i>You can keep this stuff for yourself.</i>

558
00:32:42,336 --> 00:32:44,107
<i>This time...</i>

559
00:32:44,107 --> 00:32:47,350
<i>I swear I'll protect you, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

560
00:32:53,584 --> 00:32:56,759
[Haesol High Judo Team Winter Camp]

561
00:33:21,408 --> 00:33:24,066
Agh, what are you doing?

562
00:33:38,681 --> 00:33:40,428
<i>Jung Woo Jae...</i>

563
00:33:50,184 --> 00:33:51,241
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!

564
00:33:51,241 --> 00:33:53,092
Get it together!

565
00:34:00,654 --> 00:34:02,645
[Quitters are never winners!]

566
00:34:09,587 --> 00:34:12,127
Your skills... are getting better!

567
00:34:12,127 --> 00:34:14,579
It's getting better by the minute! Good!

568
00:34:14,579 --> 00:34:17,508
- What a monster!
- That must be stressful.

569
00:34:17,508 --> 00:34:18,962
You're getting better!

570
00:34:18,962 --> 00:34:20,504
Come on, believe it!

571
00:34:20,504 --> 00:34:22,245
It's like a whole truck is on top of you.

572
00:34:22,245 --> 00:34:23,985
This is how you learn, you hear me?

573
00:34:23,985 --> 00:34:26,034
This is how you learn!

574
00:34:27,728 --> 00:34:30,259
Look, guys, Woo Jae is having
a great workout sesh!

575
00:34:32,940 --> 00:34:34,449
Yoon Ha Ru!

576
00:34:35,288 --> 00:34:36,988
You've got that glint in your eyes.

577
00:34:38,953 --> 00:34:40,484
Come here.

578
00:34:40,484 --> 00:34:41,835
Come on, hurry up.

579
00:34:41,835 --> 00:34:43,928
Looks refreshing.

580
00:34:43,928 --> 00:34:46,135
- You have to go.
- No, but...

581
00:34:46,135 --> 00:34:47,429
- Hurry up.
- You have no choice.

582
00:34:47,429 --> 00:34:48,457
- Quickly, now.
- Goodbye.

583
00:34:48,457 --> 00:34:51,107
- Hurry, now.
- Good luck!

584
00:34:51,107 --> 00:34:52,807
Yoon Ha Ru.

585
00:35:04,482 --> 00:35:06,259
What is wrong with you?

586
00:35:06,259 --> 00:35:07,676
Get out of here.

587
00:35:08,354 --> 00:35:09,531
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

588
00:35:09,531 --> 00:35:10,746
Are you alright?

589
00:35:10,746 --> 00:35:13,048
What were you thinking?

590
00:35:13,048 --> 00:35:14,269
What's the matter?

591
00:35:14,269 --> 00:35:17,871
- Did I do something wrong?
- You just got pummeled into the ground!

592
00:35:17,871 --> 00:35:19,801
He armlocked you!

593
00:35:19,801 --> 00:35:21,882
What do you think you're doing?

594
00:35:21,882 --> 00:35:24,375
What do you mean? I'm training.

595
00:35:24,375 --> 00:35:25,831
Are you injured?

596
00:35:25,831 --> 00:35:27,588
Move your shoulder like this. Does it hurt?

597
00:35:27,588 --> 00:35:29,504
Hey, look, I'm fine!

598
00:35:30,156 --> 00:35:31,180
Hey!

599
00:35:31,180 --> 00:35:32,488
Take good care of your shoulder!

600
00:35:32,488 --> 00:35:33,956
Just be gentle with it, okay?

601
00:35:33,956 --> 00:35:35,535
- Wait, what's wrong?
- Are you hurt?

602
00:35:35,535 --> 00:35:36,900
- Where?
- Is something wrong?

603
00:35:36,900 --> 00:35:38,784
I'm fine.

604
00:35:38,784 --> 00:35:40,621
- Get out of my way.
- Hey, but your shoulder...

605
00:35:40,621 --> 00:35:42,354
He's clearly injured...

606
00:35:43,488 --> 00:35:45,188
Right?

607
00:35:54,132 --> 00:35:56,346
What, is this seriously all you're eating?

608
00:35:57,045 --> 00:35:58,619
Yes. What's wrong?

609
00:35:58,619 --> 00:36:01,007
This isn't enough food for an athlete.

610
00:36:01,007 --> 00:36:02,194
I think it's perfect.

611
00:36:02,194 --> 00:36:05,286
What's up with you, man?

612
00:36:05,286 --> 00:36:06,986
No, why do you ask?

613
00:36:08,147 --> 00:36:09,492
Nothing.

614
00:36:15,794 --> 00:36:17,750
[Dad]

615
00:36:28,204 --> 00:36:29,252
Hey.

616
00:36:29,252 --> 00:36:30,496
Oh, wow, hello!

617
00:36:30,496 --> 00:36:33,647
Hi! Hi, everyone.

618
00:36:33,647 --> 00:36:35,520
Let's see...

619
00:36:36,956 --> 00:36:38,272
Here.

620
00:36:39,390 --> 00:36:41,827
What's this, Ms. Ha Na?

621
00:36:41,827 --> 00:36:43,917
Have a sip before your meal.

622
00:36:43,917 --> 00:36:45,544
You drink this, and your energy
just bursts through the roof!

623
00:36:45,544 --> 00:36:47,941
No more tiredness! Bam!
It's the good stuff, I swear.

624
00:36:47,941 --> 00:36:50,073
This is what makes a national athlete.

625
00:36:50,073 --> 00:36:52,266
National athlete? Who?

626
00:36:53,723 --> 00:36:55,654
Oh, that's...

627
00:36:55,654 --> 00:36:57,952
There's a person I know.
National athlete and gold medalist.

628
00:36:57,952 --> 00:36:59,821
- No matter, drink it, come on.
- There's a person, you hear?

629
00:36:59,821 --> 00:37:01,397
If she says there's a guy, there's a guy.

630
00:37:01,397 --> 00:37:03,101
- You'll see when you try it!
- What is it?

631
00:37:03,101 --> 00:37:04,801
What is it, huh?

632
00:37:13,502 --> 00:37:15,009
Woo Jae.

633
00:37:18,687 --> 00:37:21,048
- Me?
- Drink up.

634
00:37:41,120 --> 00:37:43,115
<i>I'm at the school. Come outside.</i>

635
00:37:43,115 --> 00:37:44,441
So tasty!

636
00:38:06,901 --> 00:38:08,421
Hey! Son!

637
00:38:08,421 --> 00:38:10,121
Son, hey! Come here!

638
00:38:19,025 --> 00:38:21,851
There are too many people around. Come with me.

639
00:38:23,441 --> 00:38:24,788
Wow, the bastard.

640
00:38:24,788 --> 00:38:27,462
So rude to his own father.

641
00:38:38,810 --> 00:38:40,945
- Where are they going?
- I don't know.

642
00:38:43,815 --> 00:38:46,489
My son. It's so hard to see you these days.

643
00:38:47,999 --> 00:38:49,658
How did you find out about this place?

644
00:38:49,658 --> 00:38:50,846
What? How did I find out?

645
00:38:50,846 --> 00:38:52,628
You know my friend, Mr. Jung Gyu, right?

646
00:38:52,628 --> 00:38:55,834
Well, he told me you were in the newspaper!

647
00:38:57,245 --> 00:38:59,135
See this? "The future of Korea.

648
00:38:59,135 --> 00:39:01,606
Rising stars of the national team..."

649
00:39:01,606 --> 00:39:02,655
And here, here. Look.

650
00:39:02,655 --> 00:39:05,241
"Haesol High, Judo Team, 11th grader...

651
00:39:05,241 --> 00:39:07,539
Jung Woo Jae."

652
00:39:08,324 --> 00:39:09,941
Now, isn't that something?

653
00:39:09,941 --> 00:39:11,718
Wow, so, whose son is that, I wonder?

654
00:39:11,718 --> 00:39:13,651
Am I right?

655
00:39:18,712 --> 00:39:20,412
So, where's your mom?

656
00:39:21,270 --> 00:39:22,581
Why do you want to know?

657
00:39:22,581 --> 00:39:23,692
"Why?"

658
00:39:23,692 --> 00:39:27,172
So I'm just supposed to let that fox
live happily ever after without me?

659
00:39:29,383 --> 00:39:31,195
I don't know.

660
00:39:31,195 --> 00:39:32,532
We haven't kept in touch for a while.

661
00:39:32,532 --> 00:39:34,899
You little liar.

662
00:39:35,497 --> 00:39:37,901
You go and tell that woman, you hear me?

663
00:39:37,901 --> 00:39:39,529
Tell her that she'll never hide from me.

664
00:39:39,529 --> 00:39:41,852
I'll find her, just you wait.

665
00:39:41,852 --> 00:39:43,103
And you.

666
00:39:43,103 --> 00:39:44,803
Got some cash?

667
00:39:48,692 --> 00:39:52,310
The article said you're
getting good financial support.

668
00:39:52,310 --> 00:39:53,948
Nothing? Really?

669
00:39:53,948 --> 00:39:55,524
Do you think I owe you anything?

670
00:39:55,524 --> 00:39:57,897
Think, now. Have you ever given me anything?

671
00:39:57,897 --> 00:40:00,531
- That's no way to talk to your dad!
- "Dad?"

672
00:40:00,531 --> 00:40:03,118
If you want me to treat you like a father,

673
00:40:03,118 --> 00:40:05,163
don't ever go looking for Mom.

674
00:40:05,812 --> 00:40:07,611
I'm warning you.

675
00:40:15,628 --> 00:40:17,878
That's everything I have.

676
00:40:17,878 --> 00:40:19,510
So just please,

677
00:40:19,510 --> 00:40:20,887
don't ever come see me again.

678
00:40:20,887 --> 00:40:23,065
Rude little rascal.

679
00:40:23,065 --> 00:40:24,508
See you.

680
00:40:38,132 --> 00:40:42,015
- Why are you making weird noises?
- This is a good stretch!

681
00:40:49,788 --> 00:40:51,910
- Come on, faster.
- Yes, sir.

682
00:40:51,910 --> 00:40:53,239
Let's go.

683
00:40:54,808 --> 00:40:56,022
Let's do 10 sets of 400.

684
00:40:56,022 --> 00:40:57,552
- Boo!
- No!

685
00:40:57,552 --> 00:40:58,993
- What even!
- Boo! Boo!

686
00:40:58,993 --> 00:41:00,017
Okay, then, 15 sets it is.

687
00:41:00,017 --> 00:41:04,344
- 10 sets is good!
- Yay, 10! We'll do our best!

688
00:41:05,822 --> 00:41:07,546
- All good?
- Yes, sir!

689
00:41:07,546 --> 00:41:10,113
If Soo Hyuk falls behind,
I'll make all of you do 4 more sets,

690
00:41:10,113 --> 00:41:12,644
so keep encouraging him, okay?

691
00:41:13,446 --> 00:41:14,724
I'll carry him on my back!

692
00:41:14,724 --> 00:41:16,537
- Pass it on.
- Ready, set...

693
00:41:26,414 --> 00:41:28,114
This is nice.

694
00:41:32,927 --> 00:41:34,505
<i>Do you think I owe you anything?</i>

695
00:41:34,505 --> 00:41:36,879
<i>Have you ever given me anything?</i>

696
00:41:36,879 --> 00:41:39,520
<i>- That's no way to talk to your dad!
- "Dad?"</i>

697
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:42,114
<i>If you want me to treat you like a father,</i>

698
00:41:42,114 --> 00:41:44,199
<i>don't ever go looking for Mom.</i>

699
00:41:47,526 --> 00:41:49,226
Time for exercise.

700
00:41:59,247 --> 00:42:02,389
I can't do anything with
Yoon Ha Na's feeble body!

701
00:42:02,389 --> 00:42:04,756
What am I supposed to do in this body?

702
00:42:07,776 --> 00:42:09,660
Think, Yoon Ha Ru.

703
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:11,634
What can I do in this situation?

704
00:42:11,634 --> 00:42:13,913
Come up with something, anything, Yoon Ha Ru!

705
00:42:14,700 --> 00:42:16,137
- Bye!
- Goodbye!

706
00:42:16,137 --> 00:42:17,221
- What are we having?
- Pork belly!

707
00:42:17,221 --> 00:42:20,148
- Grilled pork belly!
- Pork belly, pork, pork!

708
00:42:27,626 --> 00:42:29,572
Hey, what are you doing? Come out already!

709
00:42:29,572 --> 00:42:31,223
I'm coming, okay?
I think the makchang I had was bad.

710
00:42:31,223 --> 00:42:32,263
I got a bellyache.

711
00:42:32,263 --> 00:42:33,820
You're pissing me off.

712
00:42:33,820 --> 00:42:35,476
<i>It's out of my system now.</i>

713
00:42:35,476 --> 00:42:38,126
- Hey, Woo Jae, do you have time to...
- Oh!

714
00:42:38,840 --> 00:42:40,471
The walking 500 million won.

715
00:42:44,620 --> 00:42:46,732
- Woo Jae...
- Hey! Come to the back gate!

716
00:42:46,732 --> 00:42:48,092
Back gate?

717
00:42:48,092 --> 00:42:49,792
Okay, on it!

718
00:42:56,865 --> 00:42:58,905
Hey! Stop right there, money-maker!

719
00:43:04,107 --> 00:43:05,471
Hey!

720
00:43:06,398 --> 00:43:08,098
Hey! Come here!

721
00:43:17,914 --> 00:43:20,052
Why are there so many damn stairs?

722
00:43:54,024 --> 00:43:55,405
[Location information act]

723
00:43:55,405 --> 00:43:58,391
"Threatening for money is extortion,
a criminal offense..."

724
00:43:58,391 --> 00:44:01,491
"Tracking someone's location
is against the law..."

725
00:44:01,491 --> 00:44:04,336
So it's a felony, huh?

726
00:44:06,233 --> 00:44:08,275
<i>You go and tell that woman, you hear me?</i>

727
00:44:08,275 --> 00:44:09,896
<i>Tell her that she'll never hide from me.</i>

728
00:44:09,896 --> 00:44:12,205
<i>Oh, I'll find her, just you wait.</i>

729
00:44:12,205 --> 00:44:13,469
<i>And you.</i>

730
00:44:13,469 --> 00:44:15,169
<i>Got some cash?</i>

731
00:44:15,975 --> 00:44:19,060
Can he file a restraining order or something?

732
00:44:22,453 --> 00:44:24,210
[Ask a lawyer online]

733
00:44:24,210 --> 00:44:27,284
[Underage son...]

734
00:44:30,113 --> 00:44:31,415
[Beast]

735
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:34,180
Wow, that's rich.

736
00:44:34,770 --> 00:44:37,061
Yes, this is the mangy beast speaking.

737
00:44:37,061 --> 00:44:38,212
<i>So, what did you find out?</i>

738
00:44:38,212 --> 00:44:39,396
Woo Jae...

739
00:44:39,396 --> 00:44:40,717
<i>Woo Jae is...</i>

740
00:44:40,717 --> 00:44:43,162
Well? Spit it out! What's wrong with Woo Jae?

741
00:44:58,510 --> 00:45:00,210
You little...

742
00:45:04,829 --> 00:45:05,896
I'm here.

743
00:45:05,896 --> 00:45:07,596
Where are you?

744
00:45:08,697 --> 00:45:10,041
I lost them.

745
00:45:10,041 --> 00:45:11,278
They're nowhere to be seen!

746
00:45:11,278 --> 00:45:13,240
I'm certain they went this way!

747
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:16,637
Some sketchy men said
Woo Jae is worth 500 million won.

748
00:45:16,637 --> 00:45:18,487
<i>They were chasing him around, and...</i>

749
00:45:18,487 --> 00:45:20,187
What do we do?

750
00:45:20,874 --> 00:45:22,871
- Yoon Ha Na.
- Yes?

751
00:45:22,871 --> 00:45:24,779
<i>Listen carefully.</i>

752
00:45:24,779 --> 00:45:26,869
Haesol is a small city.
We'll find them sooner or later.

753
00:45:26,869 --> 00:45:28,162
Okay.

754
00:45:30,179 --> 00:45:31,879
Damn it!

755
00:45:53,751 --> 00:45:55,698
Come here, you little rat!

756
00:45:55,698 --> 00:45:57,398
Come here!

757
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:04,723
Get out of the way!

758
00:46:07,913 --> 00:46:09,613
Get over here!

759
00:46:15,540 --> 00:46:17,824
Stop there, you bastard!

760
00:46:33,573 --> 00:46:35,001
Oh, sir!

761
00:46:38,993 --> 00:46:40,693
You're dead now.

762
00:46:54,706 --> 00:46:56,406
It's been a while, huh?

763
00:47:08,932 --> 00:47:10,427
How did you find me this time?

764
00:47:10,427 --> 00:47:11,902
How did I find you?

765
00:47:11,902 --> 00:47:14,425
Well, the answer's obvious, isn't it?

766
00:47:14,425 --> 00:47:16,581
Your dad, of course!

767
00:47:16,581 --> 00:47:18,989
He literally pointed me to where you are.

768
00:47:23,401 --> 00:47:24,459
I...

769
00:47:24,459 --> 00:47:26,802
I don't want anything to do with him.

770
00:47:27,461 --> 00:47:29,941
- Just let me go.
- Wow, just wow.

771
00:47:29,941 --> 00:47:31,641
You're an athlete, right?

772
00:47:32,537 --> 00:47:34,637
You're well-recognized, too, isn't that so?

773
00:47:34,637 --> 00:47:37,473
I heard you receive good sponsorship.

774
00:47:38,957 --> 00:47:41,067
- That's not true.
- Don't lie to me.

775
00:47:41,067 --> 00:47:43,532
Your dad was boasting all about it.

776
00:47:43,532 --> 00:47:45,890
He said you'll be the one to pay us back.

777
00:47:46,811 --> 00:47:48,208
So?

778
00:47:50,110 --> 00:47:52,564
How will you repay us?

779
00:47:52,564 --> 00:47:53,777
Why would I pay for his debt?

780
00:47:53,777 --> 00:47:57,264
Why? Because your dad
told us to collect from you!

781
00:47:59,233 --> 00:48:00,974
Okay?

782
00:48:00,974 --> 00:48:04,255
If you're so talented, surely you get
sponsorships and scholarships.

783
00:48:04,255 --> 00:48:05,949
So there's all that money.

784
00:48:05,949 --> 00:48:09,708
I wonder if you get bonuses
for winning tournaments?

785
00:48:11,556 --> 00:48:15,695
Then we'll have to support him so that
he can keep winning, isn't that right?

786
00:48:15,695 --> 00:48:18,213
Make sure no one else wins, you get me?

787
00:48:18,213 --> 00:48:19,498
Well, then, sir.

788
00:48:19,498 --> 00:48:22,542
Should we break the whole Judo team's legs?

789
00:48:24,857 --> 00:48:26,828
- Shut up.
- What did you say, you little mongrel?

790
00:48:26,828 --> 00:48:28,976
Oh, look who's mad.

791
00:48:30,458 --> 00:48:32,476
Don't lay a finger on our judo team.

792
00:48:33,661 --> 00:48:36,044
So you really cherish your team, huh?

793
00:48:36,988 --> 00:48:38,036
Little boy.

794
00:48:38,036 --> 00:48:40,896
I guess you're too young to understand this,

795
00:48:40,896 --> 00:48:44,307
but you just told me your greatest weakness.

796
00:48:44,307 --> 00:48:45,535
Get it now?

797
00:48:46,343 --> 00:48:47,570
- How dare you!
- Back down.

798
00:48:47,570 --> 00:48:48,841
Hey, hey, hey. Calm down.

799
00:48:48,841 --> 00:48:50,757
Oh, you silly boy.

800
00:48:50,757 --> 00:48:52,735
You're just full of surprises, aren't you?

801
00:48:56,094 --> 00:48:57,991
Get a load of this guy!

802
00:49:01,993 --> 00:49:04,811
Oh, just wait and see. Stop copying my move!

803
00:49:04,811 --> 00:49:06,609
You little...

804
00:49:10,892 --> 00:49:12,156
Oh, this guy's funny.

805
00:49:12,156 --> 00:49:14,138
- Hey, hey. Loosen up.
- Let him go.

806
00:49:14,138 --> 00:49:16,274
- He's falling a bit short.
- Let go.

807
00:49:16,997 --> 00:49:18,312
Oh, god damn it!

808
00:49:18,312 --> 00:49:21,095
- What are you guys standing around for?
- I said let go!

809
00:49:23,982 --> 00:49:25,800
- Scared me there for a second.
- You little bastard!

810
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:28,697
- Stay down!
- Let me at him, too!

811
00:49:28,697 --> 00:49:31,869
- I'll kill you! Die! Die!
- Stop blocking!

812
00:49:33,301 --> 00:49:35,159
Hey, guys.

813
00:49:35,159 --> 00:49:37,110
- Let him stand.
- Yes, sir.

814
00:49:38,763 --> 00:49:40,829
- Get up, bastard.
- Stand up.

815
00:49:43,113 --> 00:49:45,071
You're dead now, little rat.

816
00:49:45,071 --> 00:49:47,554
Hold him there. Hold tight.

817
00:49:47,554 --> 00:49:49,254
You bastard...

818
00:49:52,570 --> 00:49:53,828
Sir!

819
00:49:55,053 --> 00:49:57,083
- What the...
- Who the hell are you?

820
00:50:07,847 --> 00:50:09,894
How dare you!

821
00:50:25,144 --> 00:50:26,844
Hey! Are you alright?

822
00:50:29,281 --> 00:50:30,595
Why are you here?

823
00:50:30,595 --> 00:50:33,030
It doesn't matter. Who are these people?

824
00:50:35,389 --> 00:50:38,214
Hey, you two. Mr. Skinny and Mr. Bald.

825
00:50:38,214 --> 00:50:39,890
Just who are you guys?

826
00:50:39,890 --> 00:50:42,605
I'm not Mr. Bald.
I'm Real Love Capital's Department Manager!

827
00:50:42,605 --> 00:50:45,948
I'm not Mr. Skinny.
I'm the Team Leader of Real Love Capital!

828
00:50:45,948 --> 00:50:48,368
Capital? Real Love?

829
00:50:48,368 --> 00:50:50,759
Wow, that's an awful name.

830
00:50:50,759 --> 00:50:53,392
I'll take skinny,
you take the bald one. Got it?

831
00:50:53,392 --> 00:50:55,644
- Okay.
- Come here, you!

832
00:50:55,644 --> 00:50:57,655
Ow, owie... blood...

833
00:50:57,655 --> 00:51:00,151
- I'm bleeding!
- Sir?

834
00:51:00,151 --> 00:51:02,078
Blood! I'm bleeding!

835
00:51:03,668 --> 00:51:05,439
I'm bleeding out! It's all sticky!

836
00:51:05,439 --> 00:51:06,607
Blood?

837
00:51:08,663 --> 00:51:10,171
This is sweat, sir!

838
00:51:10,171 --> 00:51:11,545
Sweat?

839
00:51:11,545 --> 00:51:12,646
Hey!

840
00:51:12,646 --> 00:51:13,985
- Hey!
- But it hurts!

841
00:51:13,985 --> 00:51:15,363
It's sweat, sir!

842
00:51:15,363 --> 00:51:17,540
I think my skull's fractured!

843
00:51:17,540 --> 00:51:18,681
They're running away!

844
00:51:18,681 --> 00:51:21,551
Ugh, Mommy... Mo-om!

845
00:51:21,551 --> 00:51:22,917
I have an ouchie...

846
00:51:28,052 --> 00:51:30,290
I'm about to lose it.

847
00:51:31,185 --> 00:51:33,891
Where are you, Jung Woo Jae?

848
00:51:40,083 --> 00:51:41,525
Did you find him?

849
00:51:41,525 --> 00:51:42,971
<i>Yeah.</i>

850
00:51:42,971 --> 00:51:46,660
<i>He's with me right now,
so you go on and head back to the dormitory.</i>

851
00:51:47,535 --> 00:51:49,756
- Okay.
- Bye.

852
00:52:25,877 --> 00:52:27,978
This is the worst.

853
00:52:29,379 --> 00:52:30,817
What is?

854
00:52:30,817 --> 00:52:32,844
I really...

855
00:52:32,844 --> 00:52:35,339
didn't want you to see this.

856
00:52:35,339 --> 00:52:37,923
What are you talking about, you bastard?
What does it matter?

857
00:52:37,923 --> 00:52:40,189
- Bastard?
- Are you...

858
00:52:40,832 --> 00:52:42,514
Are you embarrassed?

859
00:52:42,514 --> 00:52:45,477
Okay. Let me tell you something.

860
00:52:45,477 --> 00:52:46,586
Get this. Actually...

861
00:52:46,586 --> 00:52:49,134
I peed my pants in 2nd grade.

862
00:52:49,134 --> 00:52:50,298
Okay.

863
00:52:50,954 --> 00:52:52,089
What?

864
00:52:52,089 --> 00:52:53,517
It was sports day.

865
00:52:53,517 --> 00:52:55,409
The waiting line for the restroom was so long.

866
00:52:55,409 --> 00:52:58,042
I waited and waited,
but it just wasn't getting any shorter.

867
00:52:59,177 --> 00:53:02,098
It's a secret, okay? Nobody knows this.

868
00:53:02,098 --> 00:53:04,649
Yeah, of course I'll keep it a secret.

869
00:53:04,649 --> 00:53:06,464
So we're even?

870
00:53:06,464 --> 00:53:08,202
Or is this not enough?
You want to know something worse?

871
00:53:08,202 --> 00:53:09,414
No, no.

872
00:53:09,414 --> 00:53:11,114
I think I'm good.

873
00:53:21,801 --> 00:53:23,501
If I'm being honest...

874
00:53:24,344 --> 00:53:26,607
My dad is a real piece of work.

875
00:53:29,088 --> 00:53:32,052
I thought it all ended when I moved here,

876
00:53:35,466 --> 00:53:37,266
but I guess I can't really run from it.

877
00:53:47,409 --> 00:53:49,193
Oh, I'm sorry.

878
00:53:49,193 --> 00:53:50,937
I didn't mean to vent.

879
00:53:50,937 --> 00:53:53,294
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

880
00:53:54,761 --> 00:53:56,461
Thank you.

881
00:53:57,444 --> 00:53:59,144
Thanks for telling me.

882
00:54:01,941 --> 00:54:06,959
This is the perfect time for some soju.

883
00:54:06,959 --> 00:54:07,983
Ha Na, you...

884
00:54:07,983 --> 00:54:09,683
Do you drink?

885
00:54:11,349 --> 00:54:12,733
No, dummy.

886
00:54:12,733 --> 00:54:15,106
What I mean is, we should have
a drink together once we turn 20.

887
00:54:15,106 --> 00:54:16,816
- Oh, okay.
- Dummy!

888
00:54:16,816 --> 00:54:18,738
- Let's go!
- Okay.

889
00:54:32,106 --> 00:54:33,389
Go inside.

890
00:54:33,389 --> 00:54:35,093
Your parents must be worried.

891
00:54:35,093 --> 00:54:36,849
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

892
00:54:36,849 --> 00:54:38,549
Spend the night with me in my room.

893
00:54:39,146 --> 00:54:42,303
What? S-spend the night?

894
00:54:42,303 --> 00:54:44,050
- With you?
- Yeah.

895
00:54:45,373 --> 00:54:46,601
But...

896
00:54:46,601 --> 00:54:48,182
Your parents are home.

897
00:54:48,182 --> 00:54:50,407
I can't possibly stay the night
in your room, Ha Na.

898
00:54:52,071 --> 00:54:53,833
Oh, no, I meant Ha Ru's room.

899
00:54:53,833 --> 00:54:55,783
Spend the night over in Yoon Ha Ru's room.

900
00:54:55,783 --> 00:54:58,576
They won't let you in the dorm now, so...

901
00:54:59,180 --> 00:55:01,052
- Yeah, you're right.
- Yeah.

902
00:55:01,052 --> 00:55:02,163
Let's head in.

903
00:55:02,163 --> 00:55:03,501
Okay.

904
00:55:08,788 --> 00:55:11,648
<i>What was I even thinking?</i>

905
00:55:11,648 --> 00:55:13,141
<i>Get it together!</i>

906
00:56:18,972 --> 00:56:21,610
I want soboro bread...

907
00:56:21,610 --> 00:56:23,091
Get me some soboro bread...

908
00:56:23,091 --> 00:56:24,857
<i>Jung Woo Jae slept over at our place.</i>

909
00:56:24,857 --> 00:56:26,526
<i>He was gone when I woke up.</i>

910
00:56:26,526 --> 00:56:28,886
<i>Is he at the dormitory?</i>

911
00:56:33,554 --> 00:56:34,909
Yes?

912
00:56:35,624 --> 00:56:37,324
Good morning, sir.

913
00:56:38,945 --> 00:56:40,563
This is Woo Jae's locker, right?

914
00:56:40,563 --> 00:56:42,039
Yes, sir.

915
00:56:42,039 --> 00:56:43,838
What's going on?

916
00:56:43,838 --> 00:56:46,418
Wait, what are you doing? That's his stuff.

917
00:56:47,887 --> 00:56:50,696
He withdrew the deposit
for the dormitory and is moving out.

918
00:56:50,696 --> 00:56:52,160
He's quitting judo.

919
00:56:52,160 --> 00:56:53,860
Wait, what?

920
00:56:54,546 --> 00:56:57,317
Why won't you answer, Jung Woo Jae?

921
00:56:58,388 --> 00:57:01,348
What could possibly have happened?

922
00:57:08,504 --> 00:57:10,780
Hey, four bowls for breakfast is too much!

923
00:57:15,071 --> 00:57:16,085
What?

924
00:57:16,085 --> 00:57:17,785
Where's all the stuff gone?

925
00:57:19,124 --> 00:57:20,824
Did he leave?

926
00:57:21,633 --> 00:57:23,128
I don't know.

927
00:57:26,429 --> 00:57:28,412
What's this camcorder doing here?

928
00:57:30,328 --> 00:57:31,883
[Yoon Ha Na]

929
00:57:37,728 --> 00:57:39,428
Out of battery...

930
00:57:41,944 --> 00:57:43,741
Hey, turn the air conditioning on.

931
00:57:43,741 --> 00:57:45,242
How does that sound?

932
00:57:46,073 --> 00:57:48,862
Yoon Ha Ru, answer the phone!

933
00:58:10,879 --> 00:58:14,213
[Yoon Ha Na]

934
00:58:19,470 --> 00:58:20,896
<i>What?</i>

935
00:58:20,896 --> 00:58:23,797
<i>I'm back home... all of a sudden?</i>

936
00:58:30,646 --> 00:58:32,761
[May 25th, Monday]
<i>The award ceremony...</i>

937
00:58:32,761 --> 00:58:34,461
<i>is tomorrow?</i>

938
00:58:35,968 --> 00:58:37,033
[Woo Jae]

939
00:58:37,033 --> 00:58:38,392
[No results]

940
00:58:50,159 --> 00:58:53,646
<i>The number you have reached is not in service.</i>

941
00:59:02,091 --> 00:59:03,791
<i>- What?</i>
- Yes.

942
00:59:04,508 --> 00:59:08,058
- What? They're releasing an article?
<i>- Boss?</i>

943
00:59:08,058 --> 00:59:11,740
On the day before the award ceremony?
Those snakes.

944
00:59:11,740 --> 00:59:13,904
Ha Na's schedule will go as we planned.

945
00:59:13,904 --> 00:59:16,017
<i>I'm... me.</i>

946
00:59:16,017 --> 00:59:17,042
<i>I'm back.</i>

947
00:59:17,042 --> 00:59:18,284
As soon as the revised complaint is ready,

948
00:59:18,284 --> 00:59:20,578
I don't care if it's in the
middle of the night, just email me.

949
00:59:20,578 --> 00:59:22,389
Don't forget to CC me.

950
00:59:22,389 --> 00:59:23,413
Good.

951
00:59:23,413 --> 00:59:24,744
[Yoon Ha Na]

952
00:59:26,689 --> 00:59:28,359
<i>Where are you?</i>

953
00:59:28,359 --> 00:59:31,329
I'm at the company. Ye Rang's office.

954
00:59:31,329 --> 00:59:32,732
<i>Get over here right now.</i>

955
00:59:32,732 --> 00:59:34,497
Huh? Where are you?

956
00:59:34,497 --> 00:59:37,951
The award ceremony is tomorrow.
Where would I be other than at home?

957
00:59:37,951 --> 00:59:39,442
Ah, right, okay!

958
00:59:39,442 --> 00:59:41,345
I'll be there in a second.

959
00:59:41,345 --> 00:59:44,438
You're leaving me in the middle of a date?

960
00:59:44,438 --> 00:59:47,149
Did I just hear that right?

961
00:59:47,149 --> 00:59:50,226
Or did you seriously lose
all your common sense, Yoon Ha Ru?

962
00:59:52,471 --> 00:59:54,244
No, it's not that, I mean, it's...

963
00:59:54,244 --> 00:59:55,305
Well?

964
00:59:55,305 --> 00:59:59,251
Is there someone new
who's willing to take the lead?

965
00:59:59,251 --> 01:00:01,448
No, I swear it's nothing like that.

966
01:00:01,448 --> 01:00:04,208
But, yeah, she does take the lead, I guess.

967
01:00:06,127 --> 01:00:10,888
How am I supposed to take this, Yoon Ha Ru?

968
01:00:10,888 --> 01:00:12,588
Lovingly?

969
01:00:14,743 --> 01:00:16,443
I mean...

970
01:00:17,094 --> 01:00:18,509
It's just Ha Na.

971
01:00:18,509 --> 01:00:19,542
Huh?

972
01:00:19,542 --> 01:00:22,045
What's up with Ha Na?
Do you want me to come with?

973
01:00:22,045 --> 01:00:23,446
I'll call you when I get there!

974
01:00:23,446 --> 01:00:25,146
Love you!

975
01:00:26,477 --> 01:00:28,989
[Woo Jae is missing in both the past
and the present. What went wrong?]

976
01:00:28,989 --> 01:00:30,390
No, no.

977
01:00:30,390 --> 01:00:32,343
My friend, Woo Jae.

978
01:00:32,343 --> 01:00:33,846
[Water triggers it? Not just the Ha Na and Ha Ru,
but the camcorder needs to be wet, too]

979
01:00:33,846 --> 01:00:35,444
[How does the camcorder choose the
specific time to travel to? Is it random?]

980
01:00:35,444 --> 01:00:37,777
What do you mean, you don't know him?

981
01:00:39,285 --> 01:00:42,037
Darling, did you have too much wine?

982
01:00:42,037 --> 01:00:45,249
<i>I checked the whole list
of employees at the security agency.</i>

983
01:00:45,249 --> 01:00:47,108
<i>But I found nobody with the name Jung Woo Jae.</i>

984
01:00:47,108 --> 01:00:50,077
Alright, then. I'll call you back later.

985
01:00:50,077 --> 01:00:51,862
<i>Okay.</i>

986
01:00:51,862 --> 01:00:53,979
She says she doesn't know Woo Jae.

987
01:00:53,979 --> 01:00:56,696
Just how much did we change this time?

988
01:01:00,851 --> 01:01:03,355
Will this actually help us find the pattern?

989
01:01:03,355 --> 01:01:05,495
Are you sure about it?

990
01:01:05,495 --> 01:01:08,007
You and I, together, with the camcorder,
fall into a body of water.

991
01:01:08,007 --> 01:01:09,601
That's what triggers the time travel.

992
01:01:09,601 --> 01:01:11,317
And the time we travel to...

993
01:01:11,317 --> 01:01:14,087
is based on the videos
kept in the camcorder's memory.

994
01:01:14,087 --> 01:01:16,284
But as for the rules...

995
01:01:16,284 --> 01:01:17,867
I don't know.

996
01:01:21,665 --> 01:01:24,706
Maybe the camcorder decides?

997
01:01:24,706 --> 01:01:26,131
What?

998
01:01:27,689 --> 01:01:28,920
Think about it.

999
01:01:28,920 --> 01:01:32,826
Maybe there is no other rule,
except for the diving part.

1000
01:01:32,826 --> 01:01:34,953
Maybe it's just on the camcorder's whims...

1001
01:01:34,953 --> 01:01:36,917
So it's randomized, maybe?

1002
01:01:36,917 --> 01:01:39,675
Well, I can't say you're absolutely wrong.

1003
01:01:39,675 --> 01:01:42,749
I like it when things are simple.

1004
01:01:42,749 --> 01:01:45,047
This camcorder is giving me a headache.

1005
01:01:47,334 --> 01:01:49,355
The award ceremony is tomorrow.

1006
01:01:49,355 --> 01:01:51,185
Yeah, it is.

1007
01:01:51,185 --> 01:01:52,758
He... will be there.

1008
01:01:52,758 --> 01:01:54,458
The ceremony...

1009
01:01:57,090 --> 01:01:58,741
The ceremony...

1010
01:01:58,741 --> 01:02:00,188
Are you going?

1011
01:02:01,076 --> 01:02:02,730
- I have to.
- Don't even think about it!

1012
01:02:02,730 --> 01:02:04,265
What if he really does show up?

1013
01:02:04,265 --> 01:02:06,731
It's fine because we know he'll be there.

1014
01:02:06,731 --> 01:02:08,431
That way, I can avoid him.

1015
01:02:09,182 --> 01:02:10,882
Or maybe even catch him.

1016
01:02:11,996 --> 01:02:14,079
No, you can't. It's too dangerous.

1017
01:02:14,079 --> 01:02:15,950
I know.

1018
01:02:15,950 --> 01:02:18,493
I'm sure Woo Jae's alive somewhere.

1019
01:02:18,493 --> 01:02:21,682
Let's get that bastard tomorrow
and go find Woo Jae.

1020
01:02:27,756 --> 01:02:29,515
Then...

1021
01:02:29,515 --> 01:02:31,303
Just promise me one thing.

1022
01:02:31,969 --> 01:02:33,644
Tomorrow, at the ceremony,

1023
01:02:33,644 --> 01:02:35,556
whatever happens there...

1024
01:02:36,231 --> 01:02:38,447
promise me you'll put yourself first.

1025
01:02:38,447 --> 01:02:42,032
To me, what matters the most tomorrow
is saving you.

1026
01:02:42,032 --> 01:02:43,961
You'll have to be alive to find Woo Jae.

1027
01:02:44,595 --> 01:02:46,111
Understood?

1028
01:02:47,921 --> 01:02:49,299
Yes.

1029
01:03:12,708 --> 01:03:14,984
[Baekryong Film Awards]

1030
01:03:22,431 --> 01:03:26,206
[Congratulations on the award,
Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1031
01:03:26,206 --> 01:03:27,906
Have a nice day.

1032
01:03:32,905 --> 01:03:34,312
<i>Right now,</i>

1033
01:03:34,312 --> 01:03:35,827
<i>the clock reads half past six.</i>

1034
01:03:35,827 --> 01:03:36,993
<i>The award goes to...</i>

1035
01:03:36,993 --> 01:03:40,026
<i>Yoon Ha Na, from "I Was There in Your Night."</i>

1036
01:03:40,026 --> 01:03:41,371
<i>Congratulations.</i>

1037
01:03:41,371 --> 01:03:45,252
<i>The ceremony ends at 11.</i>

1038
01:03:48,301 --> 01:03:50,431
<i>Everyone's leaving. Let's go.</i>

1039
01:03:50,431 --> 01:03:53,557
<i>The time frame in which Woo Jae and I
were together in the waiting room...</i>

1040
01:03:53,557 --> 01:03:55,257
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

1041
01:03:55,954 --> 01:03:59,434
[Seok Min]
<i>is roughly between 11:30 and 11:40.</i>

1042
01:04:02,244 --> 01:04:03,987
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

1043
01:04:03,987 --> 01:04:05,687
He's so handsome!

1044
01:04:14,474 --> 01:04:16,505
<i>Five hours from now...</i>

1045
01:04:17,397 --> 01:04:19,421
<i>Someone...</i>

1046
01:04:19,421 --> 01:04:21,970
<i>will be pointing a knife at me.</i>

1047
01:04:30,349 --> 01:04:32,186
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

1048
01:04:32,186 --> 01:04:34,516
<i>You're not here to protect me this time,</i>

1049
01:04:39,375 --> 01:04:41,751
<i>but I've returned to this moment.</i>

1050
01:05:02,916 --> 01:05:04,463
<i>Don't be scared.</i>

1051
01:05:04,463 --> 01:05:06,501
<i>Just be yourself.</i>

1052
01:05:06,501 --> 01:05:09,305
<i>You're not here to keep me safe today.</i>

1053
01:05:09,305 --> 01:05:10,771
<i>But I...</i>

1054
01:05:42,834 --> 01:05:44,841
<i>I will survive, no matter what...</i>

1055
01:05:46,207 --> 01:05:49,443
[Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1056
01:06:14,647 --> 01:06:18,586
[Congratulations on the award,
Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1057
01:06:32,054 --> 01:06:33,721
<i>And I will save you.</i>

1058
01:06:33,721 --> 01:06:35,421
<i>Jung Woo Jae.</i>

1059
01:06:59,256 --> 01:07:00,647
<i>What is this?</i>

1060
01:07:00,647 --> 01:07:02,463
<i>The scar on his arm.</i>

1061
01:07:02,463 --> 01:07:03,713
<i>I know I saw it.</i>

1062
01:07:03,713 --> 01:07:04,770
<i>Let's go back again.</i>

1063
01:07:04,770 --> 01:07:06,116
<i>We can find him.</i>

1064
01:07:08,463 --> 01:07:10,547
<i>How much does he owe in total?</i>

1065
01:07:10,547 --> 01:07:12,598
<i>You said you'd pay me back for today.</i>

1066
01:07:12,598 --> 01:07:14,824
<i>Korea's national team judo player,
Jung Woo Jae!</i>

1067
01:07:14,824 --> 01:07:16,546
<i>Win the gold.</i>

1068
01:07:16,546 --> 01:07:17,867
<i>Something's off.</i>

1069
01:07:19,841 --> 01:07:21,731
<i>Something's really off.</i>

1070
01:07:21,731 --> 01:07:22,505
<i>Yoon Ha Na?</i>

1071
01:07:22,505 --> 01:07:24,549
<i>Jung Woo Jae, get up.</i>

1072
01:07:24,549 --> 01:07:27,422
<i>You saw the way he looked at me, right?</i>

1073
01:07:27,422 --> 01:07:30,242
<i>It was so intense, I thought I'd melt!</i>
